From 9a7168563b54d6a597d61c4e8d07b610de58accc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ParkWardRR <alfa147x@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 11:14:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 10/50] qualcommax: rename DTS to convention
 ipq8072-ews377ap-v3.dts (fixes build)

The image build derives the DTB name from the device name with the vendor
prefix stripped (engenius_ews377ap-v3 -> ipq8072-ews377ap-v3.dts), matching
in-tree devices (tplink_eap660hd-v1 -> ipq8072-eap660hd-v1.dts). The file
was misnamed with the vendor included, causing target/linux/install to fail
with 'No such file'. Content unchanged.
---
 PORT-STATUS-ews377ap-v3.md                                    | 2 +-
 ews377ap-v3-port/README.md                                    | 2 +-
 ews377ap-v3-port/porting-plan.md                              | 4 ++--
 ...q8072-engenius-ews377ap-v3.dts => ipq8072-ews377ap-v3.dts} | 0
 4 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
 rename target/linux/qualcommax/dts/{ipq8072-engenius-ews377ap-v3.dts => ipq8072-ews377ap-v3.dts} (100%)

